# Tauri / Rust Backend

> Paths below are relative to `apps/desktop/`.

Rust layer owns **all I/O**: SQLite, filesystem scans, process launch, and session tracking.
The React frontend calls Tauri commands via `src/lib/tauri.ts` — it never spawns games directly.

Product scope and command contract: [docs/DESIGN_DOC.mdc](DESIGN_DOC.mdc).

## Responsibilities

- **Database:** SQLite persistence with versioned migrations (`database/migrations.rs`).
- **Library:** CRUD for games, favorites, hidden flag, settings key/value store.
- **Importers:** Discover and import from Steam, Astris, GameHub, macOS apps, manual paths.
- **Launching:** Resolve `LaunchConfiguration`, spawn process, monitor exit, record playtime.
- **Sessions:** Track active game PID; block delete/clear while running.
- **Themes:** List, save, and delete custom JSON themes in Application Support (`services/theme_files.rs`).
- **Artwork:** Read local image files, fetch URLs, optional RAWG search, SteamGridDB enrichment cache.
- **Window:** Fullscreen toggle, hide/show Orbit during gameplay.

## Security model

- **Path validation:** Canonicalize and reject traversal before read/launch.
- **Launch whitelist:** Only launch resolved executables from importer output or validated manual paths — no arbitrary shell from frontend strings.
- **Parameterized SQL:** All queries in `database/repository.rs` use bound parameters.
- **No secrets in logs:** Avoid logging full paths with usernames, API keys, or tokens.
- **Untrusted theme JSON:** `theme_files::sanitize_theme` drops themes with invalid ids (`[a-z0-9-]`, ≤ 48 chars) or non-`R G B` colors, clips text fields, and keeps only inline `data:image/{png,jpeg,webp,gif}` images ≤ 8 MB (no remote URLs, paths, or SVG). Files over 20 MB are skipped. `save_custom_theme` / `delete_custom_theme` only touch `custom-*.json`, so the file path is always built from a validated slug.

## Tech stack

- Tauri 2
- Rust (stable)
- rusqlite (SQLite)
- serde / serde_json
- chrono (timestamps)
- anyhow (error context)

Plugins: `tauri-plugin-opener`, `tauri-plugin-dialog` (legacy; file pickers use custom command), `tauri-plugin-process`.

## Module pattern

Each domain gets its own folder. Commands stay thin — delegate to services, importers, or repository.

```
src-tauri/src/
  lib.rs                   # App bootstrap, AppState, generate_handler!
  main.rs                  # Entry point
  commands/
    mod.rs
    games.rs               # Library CRUD + settings
    dialog.rs              # pick_open_path — main-thread-safe NSOpenPanel via rfd
    session.rs             # launch_game, stop_game, get_active_session
    window.rs              # Fullscreen + hide/show
    importers.rs           # detect + scan commands (+ auto-enrich hook)
    themes.rs              # list / save / delete custom themes (thin; delegates to theme_files)
    steam.rs               # Open Steam library or native install dialog
    theme_previews.rs      # Streaming native GPU thumbnail preparation
    glass.rs               # Cached native material texture
    hero.rs                # Selected artwork lighting
    artwork.rs             # Image read/fetch/search
    metadata.rs            # enrich_game_metadata / enrich_games_metadata
  database/
    mod.rs
    migrations.rs          # Versioned schema migrations
    repository.rs          # Library SQLite access
    metadata_cache.rs      # Separate metadata enrichment cache DB
  importers/
    mod.rs
    steam.rs
    astris.rs
    gamehub.rs
    native_apps.rs
  launching/
    mod.rs
    app_launch.rs          # Shared open-app + 3s delay helpers
    context.rs             # Launch-time screen context from Orbit window
    launcher.rs            # Resolve LaunchConfiguration → Command
    gamehub_readiness.rs   # GameHub deep-link dispatch
    process_monitor.rs     # Watch child process exit
    session.rs             # SessionManager — active session state
  models/
    mod.rs
    game.rs                # Game, LaunchConfiguration, requests
    session.rs             # GameSession
    theme.rs               # ThemeDefinition, ThemeBranding
  services/
    mod.rs
    library_sync.rs        # Upsert imported games (stable_key dedup)
    metadata_enrichment.rs # TheGamesDB + SteamGridDB orchestrator
    metadata_merge.rs      # Placeholder description + artwork slot merge
    thegamesdb.rs          # TheGamesDB API client
    steamgrid.rs           # SteamGridDB API client
    artwork.rs             # Disk artwork-cache helpers
    http.rs                # Shared reqwest client + fetch_bytes
    public_artwork.rs      # RAWG / Wikimedia search + URL fetch encode
    artwork_search.rs      # Multi-provider artwork search for the picker grid / random (`logo` slot: SteamGridDB + Steam Store only)
    steam_store_artwork.rs # Steam Store images for a known app ID
    import_artwork.rs      # Guarantee every slot has art after import (generated fallback)
    theme_image_optimization.rs # Bounded custom image preparation
    theme_previews.rs      # Validated bundle inputs and disk thumbnail cache
    glass_material.rs      # One-time bounded grain rendering
    hero_lighting.rs       # Scoped local artwork sampling
    steam_library.rs       # Steam install handoff and platform check
    steam_content.rs       # Steam depot / DLC inventory helpers
    switch_library.rs      # Switch ROM library grouping
    game_content.rs        # Home content inventory aggregation
    theme_files.rs         # Theme JSON sanitization + custom theme file I/O
    theme_catalog.rs       # Worker catalog, cached custom display artwork and previews
  utils/
    mod.rs
    paths.rs               # database_path, artwork_cache_dir, app support dirs
    steam_app_id.rs        # Parse Steam app IDs from launch config / deep links
    steam_paths.rs         # Shared Steam root detection
    switch_scan.rs         # Bounded Switch ROM walk + parse
    filenames.rs           # Parse title from ROM/exe names
    size.rs                # Directory size calculation
```

| Layer | Allowed contents |
| ----- | ---------------- |
| `commands/*.rs` | `#[tauri::command]` handlers; parse args, call repo/service, map errors |
| `database/repository.rs` | SQL only — no process launch |
| `importers/*.rs` | One platform per file; returns `Vec<Game>` candidates |
| `launching/*.rs` | Process lifecycle only |
| `lib.rs` | Wiring + `AppState` — no business logic |

```rust
// ❌ BAD — command mixes import + launch + SQL inline
#[tauri::command]
async fn magic(path: String) -> Result<(), String> { /* ... */ }

// ✅ GOOD — command delegates
#[tauri::command]
pub async fn scan_steam_library(state: State<'_, AppState>) -> Result<ScanResult, String> {
    let games = SteamImporter::new(None).discover_games().await.map_err(|e| e.to_string())?;
    let upsert = LibrarySyncService::upsert_imported(&state.repo, &games).map_err(|e| e.to_string())?;
    Ok(ScanResult { imported: upsert.imported, enriched: 0, provider: "steam".into() })
}
```

## AppState

Shared state injected into commands:

```rust
pub struct AppState {
    pub repo: Arc<GameRepository>,
    pub metadata_cache: Arc<MetadataCacheRepository>,
    pub sessions: Arc<SessionManager>,
}
```

Created in `lib.rs` at startup; library DB from `utils::paths::database_path()`, metadata cache from `metadata_cache_path()`. Both repositories are opened once and shared via `AppState`.

## Database

Migrations in `database/migrations.rs` — applied sequentially via `schema_migrations` table.

### Core tables

- **games** — `id`, `stable_key` (unique dedup), `title`, `sort_title`, `provider`, `platform`,
  `source_id`, `launch_config_json`, `artwork_json`, `favorite`, `hidden`, `date_added`,
  `last_played_at`, `total_playtime_seconds`, `description`, `install_size_bytes`, `achievements_json`
- **play_sessions** — session history linked to `game_id` (indexed on `game_id`)
- **settings** — key/value JSON blobs
- **import_sources** — provider + path registry

`list_games` returns artwork-light rows (spills huge inline `data:image/...` base64 into `artwork-cache/` file paths on read/write; keeps http(s) and existing paths) and applies user overrides from a single batched query. `get_game` returns full artwork references. `upsert_imported` preloads existing `stable_key` rows once instead of per-item SELECTs.

`stable_key` prevents duplicate imports across rescans.

## Importers

| Importer | ID | Detect | Notes |
| -------- | -- | ------ | ----- |
| `SteamImporter` | `steam` | Steam install present | Reads libraryfolders, app manifests, playtime |
| `AstrisImporter` | `astris` | User folder | `.nsp` / `.xci` Nintendo Switch ROMs |
| `NativeAppImporter` | `native` | Always on macOS | `/Applications` `.app` bundles |
| `GameHubImporter` | `gamehub` | `/Applications` + `~/Applications` | Verified shortcuts only (`com.gamehub.shortcut.*` bundle id) |
| Manual | `manual` | `import_game_path` | User file picker |

Each importer implements `GameImporter` trait: `detect()`, `discover_games()`.

## Launch flow

1. Frontend calls `launch_game(gameId)`.
2. `SessionManager` loads game from repo, resolves `LaunchConfiguration`.
3. `launcher.rs` spawns the appropriate process (Steam URL, open file, open app, custom command).
   Switch `.nsp` / `.xci` launches always resolve to the **base application ROM** in the same folder; updates and DLC are left for the emulator to pick up.
   **GameHub** titles use launch type `gamehub`: open `GameHub.app`, wait 3 seconds, then spawn
   `GameHub.app/Contents/MacOS/GameHub` with the shortcut's `gamehub://` deep link. While GameHub
   boots, a macOS helper moves its window to Orbit's current monitor and toggles fullscreen.
   **Steam** titles invoke `steam://rungameid/{appId}` with the same monitor helper targeting
   `Steam`. **Astris** Switch ROMs open via `open -a Astris` when installed; a background watcher
   moves Astris onto Orbit's monitor and fullscreens it. **Native macOS apps** use the `.app`
   process name the same way.
4. PID stored; `hide_orbit_window` optional during play.
5. `process_monitor.rs` watches exit → updates playtime, ends session, `show_orbit_window`.

`delete_game` and `clear_library` reject when `sessions.get_active()` matches.

## Window configuration

`src-tauri/tauri.conf.json` configures the main window:

- `fullscreen: true` — launches into fullscreen on macOS.
- `decorations: true` with `titleBarStyle: "Transparent"` and `hiddenTitle: true` — keeps the native traffic lights but removes the title text and makes the title bar transparent so the Liquid Glass shell blends behind it.
- `transparent: true` — required for the transparent title bar and lets the webview background show through.

The frontend (`MacosShell.tsx`) sets `data-fullscreen` from the UI store; `macos.css` nudges the header brand right in windowed mode so it does not sit under the traffic lights.

